ile day07 technique log\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/mobile-android.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":22,"newStart":1,"newLines":26,"lines":["-# mobile-android — technique log (days 1-6; updated after every day)","+# mobile-android — technique log (days 1-7; updated after every day)"," "," How the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):"," - Every APK so far was the same ~12.7 KB fixture with 6 zip entries: `AndroidManifest.xml`, `assets/huntress_puzzle.json`,","   `classes.dex`, `META-INF/FIXTURE-.{SF,RSA}`, `MANIFEST.MF`. One question, `answer` = `ANS-` + 16 uppercase hex."," - Each day has a new Android IPC/security THEME, written in the manifest `<meta-data android:name=\"huntress.mechanic\">`","-  (exported Activity, permissive deep link, nested Intent, mutable PendingIntent, allowBackup, exported ContentProvider).","-  The theme was flavour only: no day required exploiting it.","+  (exported Activity, permissive deep link, nested Intent, mutable PendingIntent, allowBackup, exported ContentProvider,","+  JavaScript-interface origin trust). The theme was flavour only: no day required exploiting it, even when the","+  dex carried a matching stub class (d7 `WebViewBridge`)."," - What actually varied day to day was the `codec` of `huntress_puzzle.json` (plain, reverse, base64, xor+key, split,","-  hex). Within one day every variant (single, TT, all Mastery sets) used the same codec. The XOR key changed per variant.","+  hex, caesar+key). Within one day every variant (single, TT, all Mastery sets) used the same codec. Keys re-roll per","+  variant. Expect a not-yet-seen codec name most days: decode it from the first 4 chars, which must become `ANS-`."," - In every APK, `.ChallengeActivity` builds a device-loopback URL `http://127.0.0.1:19090/mobile/attempt/<id>/evidence?","   case_id=..&client_secret=SECRET-..&proof=<answer>`. That backend is NOT reachable (it lives on the phone). The GM","-  accepted the decoded puzzle value as the \"backend evidence code\" on all 6 days.","+  accepted the decoded puzzle value as the \"backend evidence code\" on all 7 days."," - Expect escalation (inference, see reference/HARDENING.md): the answer may move into the dex, resources or a decrypt","   routine. `lib.android.extract_answer` has the fallback chain for that case."," "," ## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)","-- **Puzzle codec** -- the same within one day, but the XOR key (and any split/offset parameters) re-roll per variant:","-  read them from `huntress_puzzle.json` every time.","+- **Puzzle codec** -- the same within one day, but `key` (xor byte d4, caesar shift d7: 10/18/9/3/4) and any","+  split/offset parameters re-roll per variant: read them from `huntress_puzzle.json` every time.","+- **Per-variant identity** -- case ref, package suffix `v<12 hex>`, `client_secret` and the loopback attempt slug","+  change per variant (all Mastery sets shared one slug on d7). APK size stays 12704 B. None of these feed the answer."," - **Mastery packaging** -- `delivery N: <name>.apk` per set, often identically named: pair by sha256."," - **Answer location** -- so far always the puzzle JSON; if it decodes to nothing, fall back to dex/resources","   (`lib.android.extract_answer` chain) rather than assuming the sample's location."]},{"oldStart":41,"oldLines":10,"newStart":45,"newLines":15,"lines":[" - `reverse`: reverse the string (`...-SNA` -> `ANS-...`)."," - `base64`: `base64 -d`."," - `hex`: `xxd -r -p`.","+- `caesar` (d7): `{data, key:int}`. Plain ASCII codepoint shift: `chr(ord(c) - key)` for EVERY char (digits and `-`","+  shift too, e.g. `KX]7` key 10 -> `ANS-`). A letters-only mod-26 ROT is wrong. Derive the sign from `data[:4]` vs `ANS-`."," - `xor`: data is base64. b64-decode, then XOR every byte with the int `key` (0-255, changes per variant)."," - `split`: `parts[]` + `order[]`, where `order[i]` is the OUTPUT SLOT of `parts[i]` (not `parts[order[i]]`). Try both","   readings and keep the one that fullmatches `ANS-`.","-- The solvers also handle base32, rot13 and a `lib.decode.peel` fallback, ready for new codecs.","+- The solvers also handle base32, rot13 and a `lib.decode.peel` fallback, ready for new codecs. `lib.android.decode_payload`","+  has NO caesar branch yet (d7 solver did it inline).","+- Unknown codec + int key: try the known-plaintext trick. `key_or_shift = f(data[:4], \"ANS-\")` (xor: byte ^; shift:","+  ord diff). A constant diff across the 4 chars names the transform at once."," "," ## Day by day"," "]},{"oldStart":96,"oldLines":11,"newStart":105,"newLines":23,"lines":["   before falling back to the day 1-5 pattern."," - Submitted at about 3 min, CORRECT first try."," ","+**Day 7 — WebView Bridge** (mechanic \"JavaScript interface origin trust\"; prompt \"Cross a challenge-owned WebView","+bridge through an untrusted origin ... Submit only the exact backend answer code\")","+- Same fixture (12704 B, 6 entries). Deep link `huntress07://webview-bridge` pathPrefix `/unlock` on exported","+  `.ChallengeActivity`; dex adds a `WebViewBridge` class (`describe`/`encode`/`getData`) that was a stub. Same loopback","+  evidence URL. All static, no backend.","+- New codec `caesar`, key 10: ASCII shift of every char by `-key`. Spotted by eye in one step (`K`-10=`A`,","+  `]`-10=`S`, `7`-10=`-`).","+- Worker flow: read triage.md + pre-extracted `assets/huntress_puzzle.json`, wrote the caesar branch into solve.py,","+  `hctf submit --from-solver`. No loopback chase, no decompile. 5 tool calls.","+- Start 13:00:10Z -> CORRECT 13:01:02Z = 52s, first try. TT (9s window) correct in 3.5s, key 18. Mastery (10s","+  window) correct in 2.3s, keys 9/3/4. Zero wrong submissions.","+"," ## GM answer conventions learned"," - One field, `answer`. Single solve and TT use id `answer`; Mastery uses `set1.answer`..`set3.answer`, one APK per set."," - Format is `ANS-` + exactly 16 UPPERCASE hex, normalization `exact`. Uppercase the hex after decoding and add no","   whitespace.","-- No mobile answer has ever been rejected (zero wrong submissions on days 1-6). The GM accepts the decoded","+- No mobile answer has ever been rejected (zero wrong submissions on days 1-7). The GM accepts the decoded","   `huntress_puzzle.json` value as the \"backend evidence code\" even though the prompt says \"invoke ... return the backend","   evidence code\"."," - Mastery feedback is per set: `{\"result\":\"accepted\",\"remaining\":N}` after each set, then `CORRECT` on the last. An"]},{"oldStart":115,"oldLines":10,"newStart":136,"newLines":13,"lines":["   instead of guessing."," - **xor codec:** `data` is base64 first, and `key` may vary per variant (int; the solvers also accept a numeric string","   or a repeating string key).","+- **caesar codec:** the shift is over raw codepoints, not the alphabet (`data` contains `]`, `` ` ``, `<`, `>` --","+  JSON-escaped as `\\u003c`/`\\u003e`, so json-load it, never regex the raw text). Keep only the candidate that","+  fullmatches `^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$`."," - **Mastery filenames** carry a literal `delivery N: ` prefix. A naive path lookup fails.","-- **6-7s timed windows** (day 2+) are dominated by start + download + submit. Solve time is about 0.1s, so do no","+- **6-10s timed windows** (day 2+; d7 TT 9s, Mastery 10s) are dominated by start + download + submit. Solve time is about 0.1s, so do no","   decompiling in-window: read the zip entry directly. Day 2 Mastery expired 8 times before Homebase routing.","-- **Don't decompile when you don't need to.** Every solve so far needed only the manifest (for context) and the asset.","+- **Don't decompile when you don't need to.** Every solve so far (d1-d7) needed only the asset; the manifest was context only.","   Keep jadx/apktool for the day the asset is missing or lacks `ANS-`."," - **Harness, not GM:** a re-start can clobber `single_solve/start.json` (no attempt_id), which