the zip). Set 1's question names that same file: read the MEMBER, never decode the whole bundle.\\n\"\n    \"- **Payload only** -- TT/single differ only in the slug and length (318 vs 333 bytes); same sentence and encoding.\")\nrep(\"| 3-digit tokens, digits 0-7 only, zero-padded (`040`, `116`) | octal: same, with `int(t,8)` |\",\n    \"| 3-digit tokens, digits 0-7 only, zero-padded (`040`, `116`) | octal: same, with `int(t,8)` |\\n\"\n    \"| `%4e%69%63...` (every char incl. letters/spaces as lowercase `%xx`, no line end) | URL decode: `python3 -c \\\"import sys,urllib.parse;print(urllib.parse.unquote(open(sys.argv[1]).read()))\\\" blob.txt`. Test `%[0-9a-f]{2}` BEFORE hex/b64 |\")\nrep(\"## GM answer conventions learned\",\n\"\"\"**Day 7: Percent Chance** (\"My address bar is having a moment\").\n- 318-byte blob, every byte percent-encoded (`%4e%69...`), ONE layer -> `urllib.parse.unquote` -> slug. Start->CORRECT 53 s, first submit.\n- Worker wrote the solver from the harness skeleton (alphabet-detected `decode_frag`: `%xx` -> binary -> dec/oct -> hex -> b64 -> rot13).\n- TT window 7 s, CORRECT at 2.4 s. Mastery 33 sets x 7 lines (+ url line), window 9 s.\n- Mastery attempt 1 failed: set1 resolved to the WHOLE zip (bundle saved as `blob-01.txt`, matched by name/sha), so unquote over all 33 members gave another set's slug fragment (`py-storm-dune-80` from set 27's `zippy-...`) -> incorrect; set26 then `expired`. After `lib.common.find_artifact` was patched to return the same-named member, attempt 2 was CORRECT (7.1 s of 9 s; the start call alone took 2.9 s).\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\"\"\")\nrep(\"- A `.txt` file that is really a ZIP (check the magic, not the extension). Prefer the exact inner member over the outer same-named container.\",\n    \"- A `.txt` file that is really a ZIP (check the magic, not the extension). Prefer the exact inner member over the outer same-named container. Day 7 mastery lost an attempt to this: set 1 decoded the whole bundle. A slug that is a word suffix (`py-...`), or a set1 answer that doesn't come from its own last line, is the tell. Dry runs on renamed per-set copies do NOT reproduce the zip-named-`blob-01.txt` layout, so test on the raw delivery.\")\nrep(\"- Timed windows (5-7 s) leave no room\",\n    \"- Timed windows (5-9 s, with GM start/submit eating 3-5 s of it) leave no room\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nwc -l reference/techniques/warmups.md; git diff --stat reference/techniques/warmups.md","description":"Apply day 7 edits to warmups log"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2170,"cache_read_input_tokens":46565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2170,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01KZJDizkK7MXeyshtQBkfKu","agent_id":"ae8546f4cf49d0350","session_id":"a2624e74-c74a-41db-9965-6b2cb921c121","uuid":"56de52f7-dd72-4e80-9082-dc61542947d7","timestamp":"2026-10-07T13:08:25.910Z","request_id":"req_011CfnvqSpprnP5Pfi9epL7P","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"warmups day07 technique log"}
