{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GN4sycb22SKmbNJjxEgoqP","type":"tool_result","content":"TOOL: {\"skill\": \"solver-authoring\"}\nTOOL: {\"command\": \"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026/challenges/day07/scripting-node-by-node && ls -la solver solver/cases solver/cases/* && wc -l solver/solve.py && cat solver/NOTES.md | head -80\"}\nUSER: Base directory for this skill: /home/testpwn/huntress-2026/.claude/skills/solver-authoring\n\n# Solver contract\n```\npython solve.py --contract <contract.json> --artifacts <dir>   ->  stdout (last line): {\"<answer_id>\": \"<value>\", ...}\n```\n- Iterate `zip(contract[\"answer_ids\"], contract[\"questions\"])`. Each question names its own `artifact` (file name inside\n  `--artifacts`, or inside an archive there). **Mastery** = several sets: `set1.x`, `set2.x`, ... each with its own\n  artifact (`blob-01.txt`, ...). It may also mix questions from earlier days. Answer every id you recognize and skip the rest\n  (the dispatcher sends other questions to other solvers).\n- Route by the question *text*, not its position: dispatch on keywords from `q[\"question\"]` and the answer-id suffix\n  (`id.split(\".\")[-1]`).\n- Apply `normalization` (`trim`, lowercase, ...) yourself.\n- Diagnostics go to stderr; only the JSON line goes to stdout. Exit non-zero with a clear message if the structure is unexpected.\n- Use only the project venv (`.venv`) plus stdlib/installed tools; subprocess calls need a `timeout`.\n- Speed matters (timed modes): no network, no heavy whole-program analysis unless it is truly needed; cache nothing between runs.\n\n# Reuse the shared library (import, don't re-derive)\nThe repo root is on PYTHONPATH, so `import lib.<x>` works from any solver. Prefer these over re-writing:\n- `lib.common` — `load_contract`, `find_artifact` (handles `container.zip -> member`, nested zips, odd names,\n  CTF passwords), `normalize`, `set_prefix` (`set1.`/`slot0_` -> unit index), `printable`.\n- `lib.decode.peel(data, accept)` — BFS layered decoder (base/hex/xor/rot/compression/zip/url/reverse) for warmups.\n- `lib.elf` — ELF `fields()`/`section_string()`/`exported_symbol()` emitting the GM's confirmed vocabulary.\n- `lib.scripts` — `deobfuscate()`, `iocs()`, `attack_for(scenario)`, `role_attack(role, language)`\n  (confirmed role->ATT&CK, e.g. `('stager','python')`->`T1105`; cmd=.003/vbs=.005/py=.006/js=.007),\n  `attack_candidates(behavior)` (reference-backed candidates for a NOVEL role). Resolve every `*-attack`\n  field from these — never hand-type a T-code. The submit guard refuses an id ATT&CK doesn't know.\n- `lib.refs.attack` — authoritative MITRE ATT&CK reference: `is_valid(id)`, `name(id)`, `tactics(id)`,\n  `id_for_name(name)`, `search(behavior)`. Use it to VALIDATE any attack value and to generate candidates\n  for an unseen role/scenario; the GM still judges correctness on submit.\n- `lib.k\nRES: solver:\ntotal 136\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 testpwn testpwn  4096 Oct  7 21:01 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 7 testpwn testpwn  4096 Oct  7 21:03 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 testpwn testpwn  4096 Oct  7 21:01 __pycache__\n-rw-r--r-- 1 testpwn testpwn 27836 Oct  7 21:01 bashplan.py\n-rw-r--r-- 1 testpwn testpwn 17364 Oct  7 21:01 batchplan.py\ndrwxr-xr-x 7 testpwn testpwn  4096 Oct  7 21:03 cases\n-rw-r--r-- 1 testpwn testpwn  1952 Oct  7 21:01 jsdecode.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 testpwn testpwn  8073 Oct  7 21:01 powerplay.py\n-rw-r--r-- 1 testpwn testpwn  9427 Oct  7 21:01 pyplan.py\n-rw-r--r-- 1 testpwn testpwn 25094 Oct  7 21:03 solve.py\n-rw-r--r-- 1 testpwn testpwn 19111 Oct  7 21:01 vbsplan.py\n\nsolver/cases:\ntotal 28\ndrwxr-xr-x 7 testpwn testpw\nTOOL: {\"command\": \"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026 && source bin/env.sh >/dev/null 2>&1; cd challenges/day07/scripting-node-by-node/solver; for c in cases/*; do echo \\\"== $c\\\"; ls $c/artifacts; done; timeout 20 python3 solve.py --contract cases/variant-time_trial-26b7da83/contract.json --artifacts cases/variant-time_trial-26b7da83/artifacts 2>&1 | tail -20\"}\nRES: == cases/single_solve\nevidence.zip\n== cases/variant-time_trial-26b7da83\nevidence.zip\n== cases/variant-time_trial-49b73141\nevidence.zip\n== cases/variant-time_trial-5ab8013f\nevidence.zip\n== cases/variant-time_trial-7d6f8d53\nevidence.zip\nno value nodejs-uploader-steps steps\nnode-local-dispatch.mjs {}\nno value nodejs-launcher-adapter adapter\nno value nodejs-launcher-campaign campaign\nno value nodejs-launcher-file-path ind:file_path\nno value nodejs-launcher-stage-count stage-count\nno value nodejs-launcher-steps steps\nnode-schedule-descriptor.mjs {}\nno value nodejs-persistence-adapter adapter\nno value nodejs-persistence-campaign campaign\nno value nodejs-persistence-schedule-path ind:schedule_path\n\nTOOL: {\"command\": \"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026/challenges/day07/scripting-node-by-node/solver; timeout 20 python3 solve.py --contract cases/variant-time_trial-26b7da83/contract.json --artifacts cases/variant-time_trial-26b7da83/artifacts 2>&1 | head -20; for c in single_solve variant-time_trial-5ab8013f variant-time_trial-26b7da83; do echo \\\"== $c\\\"; 7z l -pinfected cases/$c/artifacts/evidence.zip | tail -n +15 | head -80; done\"}\nRES: failed evidence.zip -> resource-sample.ps1 ValueError('no JSON descriptor found')\nno value resource-scenario scenario\nno value resource-attack attack\nno value resource-url url\nno value resource-wallet wallet\nno value resource-mutex mutex\nfailed evidence.zip -> collection-sample.ps1 ValueError('no JSON descriptor found')\nno value collection-scenario scenario\nno value collection-attack attack\nno value collection-url url\nno value collection-file file\nno value collection-user-agent agent\nfailed evidence.zip -> impact-sample.ps1 ValueError('no JSON descriptor found')\nno value impact-scenario scenario\nno value impact-attack attack\nno value impact-extension extension\nno value impact-note note\nno va\nTOOL: {\"command\": \"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026/challenges/day07/scripting-node-by