{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GowHEyTTqvwPAaeax8xqou","type":"tool_result","content":"def _uniq(xs):\n    seen, out = set(), []\n    for x in xs:\n        if x not in seen:\n            seen.add(x)\n            out.append(x)\n    return out\n\n\ndef attack_for(scenario):\n    \"\"\"Confirmed ATT&CK technique id for a scenario label, or None.\"\"\"\n    return K.SCENARIO_ATTACK.get(scenario)\n\n\n# Unified role -> ATT&CK resolver across scripting languages (the per-language tables in lib/knowledge.py).\n# Execution-type roles differ by interpreter: cmd=.003, Unix shell=.004, VBScript=.005, Python=.006, JavaScript=.007.\n_ROLE_TABLES = {\n    \"bash\": K.BASH_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED, \"sh\": K.BASH_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED, \"shell\": K.BASH_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED,\n    \"jscript\": K.JSCRIPT_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED, \"javascript\": K.JSCRIPT_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED,\n    \"js\": K.JSCRIPT_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED,\n    \"batch\": K.BATCH_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED, \"cmd\": K.BATCH_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED,\n    \"bat\": K.BATCH_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED,\n    \"vbs\": K.VBS_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED, \"vbscript\": K.VBS_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED,\n    \"python\": K.PY_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED, \"py\": K.PY_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED,\n}\n\n\ndef role_attack(role, language):\n    \"\"\"GM-confirmed ATT&CK id for a (role, language) scripting construct, e.g. ('stager','python') -> 'T1105',\n    ('launcher','batch') -> 'T1059.003'. Returns the id, 'none' (benign), or None when the role is unknown for\n    that language — in which case the caller falls back to the scenario mapping or attack_candidates().\"\"\"\n    return (_ROLE_TABLES.get(str(language).lower()) or {}).get(role)\n\n\ndef attack_candidates(behavior, limit=5, tactic=None):\n    \"\"\"Reference-backed candidate ATT&CK ids for a free-text behavior, for a NOVEL role/scenario with no\n    confirmed mapping (new day/lane). Candidates only — the GM validates on submit. Weak for non-literal\n    technique names; prefer the confirmed tables above. Returns [(id, name, score), ...].\"\"\"\n    try:\n        from lib.refs import attack\n        return attack.search(behavior, limit=limit, tactic=tactic)\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 - reference optional\n        return []\n        if looks_like_technique(s):\n            if not info(s):  # id-shaped but unknown to ATT&CK -> almost certainly wrong\n                bad.append((aid, s, \"not a known ATT&CK technique id\"))\n        elif is_attack_field and s.lower() not in (\"none\", \"\"):\n            bad.append((aid, s, \"attack field value is not an ATT&CK technique id or 'none'\"))\n    return bad\n\n\ndef audit_knowledge():\n    \"\"\"Validate every ATT&CK id in lib/knowledge.py's confirmed role/scenario tables against this reference.\n    Returns [(table, key, id, problem)]; empty = clean. Run as: python3 -m lib.refs.attack\"\"\"\n    from lib import knowledge as K\n    tables = {\n        \"SCENARIO_ATTACK\": getattr(K, \"SCENARIO_ATTACK\", {}),\n        \"JSCRIPT_ROLE\": getattr(K, \"JSCRIPT_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED\", {}),\n        \"BATCH_ROLE\": getattr(K, \"BATCH_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED\", {}),\n        \"VBS_ROLE\": getattr(K, \"VBS_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED\", {}),\n        \"PY_ROLE\": getattr(K, \"PY_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED\", {}),\n    }\n    bad = []\n    for tname, t in tables.items():\n        for key, tid in t.items():\n            if tid == \"none\":\n                continue\n            if not info(tid):\n                bad.append((tname, key, tid, \"unknown ATT&CK id\"))\n            elif not is_valid(tid):\n                bad.append((tname, key, tid, \"deprecated/revoked\"))\n    return bad\n\n\ndef search(behavior, limit=5, tactic=None):\n    \"\"\"Rank candidate technique ids for a free-text behavior description (e.g. 'downloads a payload over http').\n    Scores token overlap against each technique's name (weighted) + description. Optional tactic filter\n    (e.g. 'command-and-control'). Returns [(id, name, score), ...] best first — candidates, not an answer.\"\"\"\n    q = set(_tokens(behavior))\n             \"FUNCTION-style of the named function: `function f(` = declaration, `var f = function(` = \"\n             \"anonymous_expression, `var f = function f_body(` = named_expression. INVOCATION-style = how the \"\n             \"recover/inspect body invokes the next top-level function: plain `f(x)` = direct, `f.call(..)` (also via a \"\n             \"local `invoke` helper that does `block.call`) = call, `f.apply(..)` = apply. PROPERTY-style of the \"\n             \"descriptor reads: only `o.k` = dot, only `o[\\\"k\\\"]` = bracket_literal, both = mixed.\",\n        confirmed=(\"declaration\", \"named_expression\", \"anonymous_expression\", \"direct\", \"call\", \"apply\", \"dot\",\n                   \"bracket_literal\", \"mixed\"),\n        closed=True, examples=(\"var decode_x = function decode_x_body(s)->named_expression\",\n                               \"invoke.call(null, decode_x, s)->call\", \"o.steps + o[\\\"adapter\\\"]->mixed\"),\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(SCRIPT,), families=(\"attack\",),\n        rule=\"MITRE ATT&CK technique id from the step-graph ROLE. Execution roles map to the host language: batch \"\n             \"launcher/staged_chain=T1059.003, JScript launcher/staged_chain=T1059.007, VBScript launcher/staged_chain=\"\n             \"=T1059.005, bash=T1059.004, python=T1059.006, powershell=T1059.001. A graph ending in a \"\n             \"handoff is `staged_chain` even if next_stage is a .js file (not 'relay').\",\n        rejected=tuple(sum((list(v) for v in K.JSCRIPT_ATTACK_REJECTED.values()), [])) + (\"T1005\", \"T1560\", \"T1119\"),\n        examples=(\"batch launcher->T1059.003\", \"jscript staged_chain->T1059.007\", \"vbscript launcher->T1059.005\",\n                  \"downloader/stager->T1105\", \"dropper->T1140\", \"uploader->T1041\", \"impact->T1486\"),\n    ),\n]\n\n\nENUM_NOTE = (\n    \"FIRST check each question's `answer_format.kind`. If it is `enum`, the GM HANDS you the closed vocabulary in \"\n    \"`accepted_values` — pick the right one from that list, NEVER probe or guess its spelling (role, scenario, and \"\n    \"true/false fields are all enums). If it is `mitre_attack_id`, submit a `T####`/`T####.###` id (literal `none` \"\n    \"only if permitted). The HARD labels below are always `exact_text` (no list given) — those are the ones that need \"\n    \"the derivation rule + `hctf labels`.\")\n\n\n# The GM's exact_text labels are a small `<short-keyword>_<suffix>` algebra composed from real spec/keyword tokens in\n# the bytes — NEVER an analyst's descriptive synonym. Encoding the LAWS (not just per-family lists) lets a worker\n# derive the spelling of a NEW construct/host-language before it costs a clock. Proven on pe_cli, if_guard, error_guard.\nNAMING_LAWS = (\n    \"\\nGenerator naming LAWS — when an exact_text label is REJECTED, DERIVE the next spelling from these; do NOT \"\n    \"brainstorm descriptive synonyms (every synonym below was GM-rejected):\\n\"\n    \"- `<keyword>_guard`: a conditional / error bail-out is named by the SHORT language keyword that opens it — batch \"\n    \"`if errorlevel`->errorlevel_guard, batch `if defined`->if_guard, VBS `On Error Resume Next`->error_guard. The \"\n    \"spelled-out statement is ALWAYS wrong (if_defined, on_error_resume, defined_guard, flag_guard rejected).\\n\"\n    \"- `<keyword>_once`: a run-once loop = loop keyword + `_once` — Do..Exit Do->do_once, While..Wend->while_once, \"\n    \"`For p=0 To 0`->for_once (do_exit/while_wend/for_next rejected).\\n\"\n    \"- control transfer = `<keyword>_<action>`: `goto :L`->goto_dispatch, `call :L`->call_subroutine.\\n\"\n    \"- format = container[_runtime]: native = container only (elf/pe/macho); managed = container + the real runtime-spec \"\n    \"token (.NET PE = pe_cli, from PE + ECMA-335 CLI); msil/dotnet/managed/cil all rejected.\\n\"\n    \"- representation = `<numbase>_<separator-name>` (decimal_pipe, hex_colon) or `<base64|hex>_<variant>`; transform is \"\n    \"named for the ENCODE direction (subtract_modulo_256 decodes by ADDING).\\n\"\n    \"- ATT&CK execution role scales by host language: launcher/staged_chain -> T1059.{003 batch, 004 bash, \"\n    \"005 vbscript, 006 python, 007 jscript, 001 powershell}; downloader/stager T1105, dropper T1140, uploader T1041, impact T1486.\")\n\n\ndef for_lane(lane):\n    \"\"\"Markdown block for the worker prompt: the label grammar it needs for THIS lane's synthetic fields.\"\"\"\n    es = entries_for_lane(lane)\n    if not es:\n        return (ENUM_NOTE + \"\\nNo exact_text synthetic-label family is known for this lane: its remaining answers are \"\n                \"derived VALUES (hashes, decoded strings, manifest fields) in canonical form — derive from the bytes.\")\n    lines = [ENUM_NOTE,\n             \"Field-label playbook for this lane's exact_text labels (generator vocabulary — match the RULE, do not \"\n             \"guess synonyms; resolve with `hctf labels` which already seeds from these):\"]\n    for e in es:\n        fam = \"/\".join(e.families)\n        line = f\"- **{fam}**: {e.rule}\"\n        if e.confirmed:\n            line += f\" Confirmed{' (CLOSED set)' if e.closed else ''}: {', '.join(e.confirmed)}.\"\n        rej = sorted(set(e.rejected) - set(e.confirmed))\n        if rej:\n            line += f\" Already REJECTED (never resubmit): {', '.join(rej[:14])}.\"\n        if e.examples:\n            line += f\" e.g. {'; '.join(e.examples)}.\"\n        lines.append(line)\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + NAMING_LAWS","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a2624e74-c74a-41db-9965-6b2cb921c121","uuid":"5d971388-d1bc-403b-911e-ed065d512b31","timestamp":"2026-10-07T13:08:28.771Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"def _uniq(xs):\n    seen, out = set(), []\n    for x in xs:\n        if x not in seen:\n            seen.add(x)\n            out.append(x)\n    return out\n\n\ndef attack_for(scenario):\n    \"\"\"Confirmed ATT&CK technique id for a scenario label, or None.\"\"\"\n    return K.SCENARIO_ATTACK.get(scenario)\n\n\n# Unified role -> ATT&CK resolver across scripting languages (the per-language tables in lib/knowledge.py).\n# Execution-type roles differ by interpreter: cmd=.003, Unix shell=.004, VBScript=.005, Python=.006, JavaScript=.007.\n_ROLE_TABLES = {\n    \"bash\": K.BASH_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED, \"sh\": K.BASH_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED, \"shell\": K.BASH_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED,\n    \"jscript\": K.JSCRIPT_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED, \"javascript\": K.JSCRIPT_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED,\n    \"js\": K.JSCRIPT_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED,\n    \"batch\": K.BATCH_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED, \"cmd\": K.BATCH_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED,\n    \"bat\": K.BATCH_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED,\n    \"vbs\": K.VBS_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED, \"vbscript\": K.VBS_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED,\n    \"python\": K.PY_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED, \"py\": K.PY_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED,\n}\n\n\ndef role_attack(role, language):\n    \"\"\"GM-confirmed ATT&CK id for a (role, language) scripting construct, e.g. ('stager','python') -> 'T1105',\n    ('launcher','batch') -> 'T1059.003'. Returns the id, 'none' (benign), or None when the role is unknown for\n    that language — in which case the caller falls back to the scenario mapping or attack_candidates().\"\"\"\n    return (_ROLE_TABLES.get(str(language).lower()) or {}).get(role)\n\n\ndef attack_candidates(behavior, limit=5, tactic=None):\n    \"\"\"Reference-backed candidate ATT&CK ids for a free-text behavior, for a NOVEL role/scenario with no\n    confirmed mapping (new day/lane). Candidates only — the GM validates on submit. Weak for non-literal\n    technique names; prefer the confirmed tables above. Returns [(id, name, score), ...].\"\"\"\n    try:\n        from lib.refs import attack\n        return attack.search(behavior, limit=limit, tactic=tactic)\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 - reference optional\n        return []\n        if looks_like_technique(s):\n            if not info(s):  # id-shaped but unknown to ATT&CK -> almost certainly wrong\n                bad.append((aid, s, \"not a known ATT&CK technique id\"))\n        elif is_attack_field and s.lower() not in (\"none\", \"\"):\n            bad.append((aid, s, \"attack field value is not an ATT&CK technique id or 'none'\"))\n    return bad\n\n\ndef audit_knowledge():\n    \"\"\"Validate every ATT&CK id in lib/knowledge.py's confirmed role/scenario tables against this reference.\n    Returns [(table, key, id, problem)]; empty = clean. Run as: python3 -m lib.refs.attack\"\"\"\n    from lib import knowledge as K\n    tables = {\n        \"SCENARIO_ATTACK\": getattr(K, \"SCENARIO_ATTACK\", {}),\n        \"JSCRIPT_ROLE\": getattr(K, \"JSCRIPT_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED\", {}),\n        \"BATCH_ROLE\": getattr(K, \"BATCH_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED\", {}),\n        \"VBS_ROLE\": getattr(K, \"VBS_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED\", {}),\n        \"PY_ROLE\": getattr(K, \"PY_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED\", {}),\n    }\n    bad = []\n    for tname, t in tables.items():\n        for key, tid in t.items():\n            if tid == \"none\":\n                continue\n            if not info(tid):\n                bad.append((tname, key, tid, \"unknown ATT&CK id\"))\n            elif not is_valid(tid):\n                bad.append((tname, key, tid, \"deprecated/revoked\"))\n    return bad\n\n\ndef search(behavior, limit=5, tactic=None):\n    \"\"\"Rank candidate technique ids for a free-text behavior description (e.g. 'downloads a payload over http').\n    Scores token overlap against each technique's name (weighted) + description. Optional tactic filter\n    (e.g. 'command-and-control'). Returns [(id, name, score), ...] best first — candidates, not an answer.\"\"\"\n    q = set(_tokens(behavior))\n             \"FUNCTION-style of the named function: `function f(` = declaration, `var f = function(` = \"\n             \"anonymous_expression, `var f = function f_body(` = named_expression. INVOCATION-style = how the \"\n             \"recover/inspect body invokes the next top-level function: plain `f(x)` = direct, `f.call(..)` (also via a \"\n             \"local `invoke` helper that does `block.call`) = call, `f.apply(..)` = apply. PROPERTY-style of the \"\n             \"descriptor reads: only `o.k` = dot, only `o[\\\"k\\\"]` = bracket_literal, both = mixed.\",\n        confirmed=(\"declaration\", \"named_expression\", \"anonymous_expression\", \"direct\", \"call\", \"apply\", \"dot\",\n                   \"bracket_literal\", \"mixed\"),\n        closed=True, examples=(\"var decode_x = function decode_x_body(s)->named_expression\",\n                               \"invoke.call(null, decode_x, s)->call\", \"o.steps + o[\\\"adapter\\\"]->mixed\"),\n    ),\n    PlaybookEntry(\n        lanes=(SCRIPT,), families=(\"attack\",),\n        rule=\"MITRE ATT&CK technique id from the step-graph ROLE. Execution roles map to the host language: batch \"\n             \"launcher/staged_chain=T1059.003, JScript launcher/staged_chain=T1059.007, VBScript launcher/staged_chain=\"\n             \"=T1059.005, bash=T1059.004, python=T1059.006, powershell=T1059.001. A graph ending in a \"\n             \"handoff is `staged_chain` even if next_stage is a .js file (not 'relay').\",\n        rejected=tuple(sum((list(v) for v in K.JSCRIPT_ATTACK_REJECTED.values()), [])) + (\"T1005\", \"T1560\", \"T1119\"),\n        examples=(\"batch launcher->T1059.003\", \"jscript staged_chain->T1059.007\", \"vbscript launcher->T1059.005\",\n                  \"downloader/stager->T1105\", \"dropper->T1140\", \"uploader->T1041\", \"impact->T1486\"),\n    ),\n]\n\n\nENUM_NOTE = (\n    \"FIRST check each question's `answer_format.kind`. If it is `enum`, the GM HANDS you the closed vocabulary in \"\n    \"`accepted_values` — pick the right one from that list, NEVER probe or guess its spelling (role, scenario, and \"\n    \"true/false fields are all enums). If it is `mitre_attack_id`, submit a `T####`/`T####.###` id (literal `none` \"\n    \"only if permitted). The HARD labels below are always `exact_text` (no list given) — those are the ones that need \"\n    \"the derivation rule + `hctf labels`.\")\n\n\n# The GM's exact_text labels are a small `<short-keyword>_<suffix>` algebra composed from real spec/keyword tokens in\n# the bytes — NEVER an analyst's descriptive synonym. Encoding the LAWS (not just per-family lists) lets a worker\n# derive the spelling of a NEW construct/host-language before it costs a clock. Proven on pe_cli, if_guard, error_guard.\nNAMING_LAWS = (\n    \"\\nGenerator naming LAWS — when an exact_text label is REJECTED, DERIVE the next spelling from these; do NOT \"\n    \"brainstorm descriptive synonyms (every synonym below was GM-rejected):\\n\"\n    \"- `<keyword>_guard`: a conditional / error bail-out is named by the SHORT language keyword that opens it — batch \"\n    \"`if errorlevel`->errorlevel_guard, batch `if defined`->if_guard, VBS `On Error Resume Next`->error_guard. The \"\n    \"spelled-out statement is ALWAYS wrong (if_defined, on_error_resume, defined_guard, flag_guard rejected).\\n\"\n    \"- `<keyword>_once`: a run-once loop = loop keyword + `_once` — Do..Exit Do->do_once, While..Wend->while_once, \"\n    \"`For p=0 To 0`->for_once (do_exit/while_wend/for_next rejected).\\n\"\n    \"- control transfer = `<keyword>_<action>`: `goto :L`->goto_dispatch, `call :L`->call_subroutine.\\n\"\n    \"- format = container[_runtime]: native = container only (elf/pe/macho); managed = container + the real runtime-spec \"\n    \"token (.NET PE = pe_cli, from PE + ECMA-335 CLI); msil/dotnet/managed/cil all rejected.\\n\"\n    \"- representation = `<numbase>_<separator-name>` (decimal_pipe, hex_colon) or `<base64|hex>_<variant>`; transform is \"\n    \"named for the ENCODE direction (subtract_modulo_256 decodes by ADDING).\\n\"\n    \"- ATT&CK execution role scales by host language: launcher/staged_chain -> T1059.{003 batch, 004 bash, \"\n    \"005 vbscript, 006 python, 007 jscript, 001 powershell}; downloader/stager T1105, dropper T1140, uploader T1041, impact T1486.\")\n\n\ndef for_lane(lane):\n    \"\"\"Markdown block for the worker prompt: the label grammar it needs for THIS lane's synthetic fields.\"\"\"\n    es = entries_for_lane(lane)\n    if not es:\n        return (ENUM_NOTE + \"\\nNo exact_text synthetic-label family is known for this lane: its remaining answers are \"\n                \"derived VALUES (hashes, decoded strings, manifest fields) in canonical form — derive from the bytes.\")\n    lines = [ENUM_NOTE,\n             \"Field-label playbook for this lane's exact_text labels (generator vocabulary — match the RULE, do not \"\n             \"guess synonyms; resolve with `hctf labels` which already seeds from these):\"]\n    for e in es:\n        fam = \"/\".join(e.families)\n        line = f\"- **{fam}**: {e.rule}\"\n        if e.confirmed:\n            line += f\" Confirmed{' (CLOSED set)' if e.closed else ''}: {', '.join(e.confirmed)}.\"\n        rej = sorted(set(e.rejected) - set(e.confirmed))\n        if rej:\n            line += f\" Already REJECTED (never resubmit): {', '.join(rej[:14])}.\"\n        if e.examples:\n            line += f\" e.g. {'; '.join(e.examples)}.\"\n        lines.append(line)\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + NAMING_LAWS","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016umHrwaZd9WNAtXyG2z3Y7","type":"tool_result","content":"130 reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md\ndiff --git a/reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md b/reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md\nindex c10c002..4b81fae 100644\n--- a/reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md\n+++ b/reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md\n@@ -1,20 +1,26 @@\n-# metadata-forensics — technique log (days 1-6; updated after every day)\n+# metadata-forensics — technique log (days 1-7; updated after every day)\n \n How this lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n - Every day = ONE evidence zip (`metadata-day-NN-evidence.zip`, plain Deflate, no password so far) holding a tiny member\n-  (33 B - 3 KB). The question asks ONE structural fact about a named member, read from the raw bytes.\n+  (33 B - 3 KB). The question asks ONE structural fact about a named member, read from the raw bytes. The member can\n+  itself be a container (Day 7: the member was a ZIP and the field was that ZIP's own EOCD record).\n - A new `<fmt>.<field>` family each day: identity (name/size/hashes) -> magic prefix -> `text.utf8_bom_present` ->\n-  `jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels` -> `png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels` -> `pdf.header_version`. Since Day 3 the question literally\n-  names the field (`Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`); answer ids read `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>`.\n+  `jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels` -> `png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels` -> `pdf.header_version` -> `zip.eocd_total_entries`.\n+  Since Day 3 the question literally names the field (`Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`); answer ids read\n+  `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>` (`.`/`_` -> `-`, e.g. `d07-zip-001-zip-eocd-total-entries`).\n - The prompt's flavor text describes decoys (impostors, renamed copies, \"-with-bom\" names, EXIF/presentation lies, chunk\n   \"passengers\", catalog /Version overrides). The asked field so far was always the STRUCTURAL truth from the header bytes;\n-  names/extensions/secondary metadata are the lie. All 6 single solves were first-submit CORRECT in ~30-40 s.\n+  names/extensions/secondary metadata are the lie. All 7 single solves were first-submit CORRECT in ~30-60 s.\n+- Titles are puns, not format hints: Day 7 \"Seven-Zip, No Relation\" was plain ZIP (PKWARE), no .7z anywhere.\n \n ## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n - **Delivery layout** -- see \"Delivery layouts seen\" below; resolve the named member through whatever wrapper arrives.\n - **Decoys** -- renamed copies, misleading extensions/names, secondary metadata (EXIF, catalog /Version) that disagree\n   with the header: always answer from the structural header bytes of the member the question names.\n-- **Member and values** -- names, sizes and dimensions re-roll per variant; nothing about the sample is constant.\n+- **Member and values** -- names, sizes, dimensions and counts re-roll per variant; nothing about the sample is\n+  constant (Day 7 entry count went 2/3/4/5 with drop number 001-004; member names `room-NN/item-K.txt`).\n+- **Nesting depth** -- the asked file may sit 2-3 zips deep (Mastery D7: outer -> `...-evidence-0N.zip` ->\n+  `evidence-drop-00N.zip`); resolve by the name after `->`, never answer from an enclosing zip.\n \n ## Recognition cues -> first move\n | You see | First move |\n@@ -25,6 +31,7 @@ How this lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n | `text.*_bom_present` | `xxd -l 4`: UTF-8 BOM = `ef bb bf` (UTF-16LE `ff fe`, BE `fe ff`, UTF-32LE `ff fe 00 00`) -> `true`/`false` |\n | `jpeg.*dimensions*` / SOF | walk JPEG segments from `ffd8` by length to SOFn (`ffc0..ffcf` minus c4/c8/cc): P, Y=height, X=width. `exiftool -ImageSize` cross-check only |\n | `png.ihdr_*` / \"walk their chunks\" | `xxd -s 16 -l 8` = IHDR width,height (BE u32). Chunk walk = len/type/data/CRC loop (`lib.stego.png_chunks`) |\n+| `zip.eocd_*` / \"count what the archives claim\" | of the NAMED inner zip (not the evidence zip): last `PK\\x05\\x06` whose comment len reaches EOF; u16 @+8 disk entries, @+10 total, u32 @+12 cd size, @+16 cd offset, u16 @+20 comment len. `0xFFFF` -> ZIP64 locator `PK\\x06\\x07` (EOCD-20) -> `PK\\x06\\x06` u64 @+32. Cross-check: count `PK\\x01\\x02` walking from cd offset, `PK\\x03\\x04` |\n | `pdf.header_version` / \"declared versions\" | `head -c 16 <f> | xxd` -> `%PDF-x.y` at offset 0; `grep -a -o '/Version[^/>]*'` only as a diagnostic |\n | \"impostor\", \"renamed\", \"disguise\" | trust magic bytes at offset 0; a matching string deeper in the file is a decoy |\n | answer_format syntax \"use the literal none only when the requested field is absent\" | field missing (e.g. no header) -> `none` |\n@@ -75,6 +82,16 @@ only one present in single; TT used `roster.csv`, Mastery a renamed `evidence-no\n - Pre-fetched mastery contract.json listed document-003/004; the live attempt asked 006/007 -> read the live start.\n - CORRECT ~34 s; TT in_window 2.7 s (GM start call itself took 23 s that day — latency is outside the window).\n \n+**Day 7 — Seven-Zip, No Relation** (ZIP EOCD census). `zip.eocd_total_entries` integer, id `d07-zip-001-zip-eocd-total-entries`.\n+- Evidence zip held `evidence-drop-001.zip` (410 B, Stored, data-descriptor flag) with `room-01/item-1.txt`,\n+  `room-02/item-1.txt` (identical 48 B text). EOCD total-entries u16 @+10 = 2 -> answer `2` (base-10, no units).\n+- All variants were honest: EOCD disk/total == CD headers == LFHs, no comment/trailing bytes. The prompt's \"empty space\"\n+  / \"census that does not add up\" (claim vs real walk, padding, dir entries) was flavor only — not exercised, so it is\n+  still unknown whether the GM wants the claimed or the walked count when they differ. Answer the field = the CLAIM.\n+- Worker: `xxd | tail` + `7z l -slt` on triage's pre-extracted inner zip, then stdlib `struct` EOCD parser in solve.py\n+  (ZIP64 aware). CORRECT 57 s after start, first try. TT 3 entries (in_window 0.89 s / 7 s); Mastery set1 4, set2 5\n+  (1.33 s / 7 s). Pre-fetched mastery contract (003/004) matched live this time.\n+\n ## GM answer conventions learned\n - Filenames: exact base name incl. extension, no directory. Sizes: base-10 integer, no units. Hashes: hex, case ignored.\n - Byte prefixes: lowercase hex, contiguous, exactly 2N chars (`xxd -p -l N`).\n@@ -82,7 +99,8 @@ only one present in single; TT used `roster.csv`, Mastery a renamed `evidence-no\n - Pixel dimensions (JPEG SOF, PNG IHDR): `<width>x<height>` — width first, lowercase `x`, no spaces (GM-confirmed both).\n - PDF header version: bare `x.y` from the leading `%PDF-x.y` (no `PDF-`/`%` prefix); absent header -> literal `none`\n   (contract wording; `none` itself not yet GM-confirmed).\n-- Rejected spellings: none recorded in this lane (no wrong submission in any mode, days 1-6).\n+- Counts (`zip.eocd_total_entries`): plain base-10 integer string, e.g. `2` (GM-confirmed D7 single/TT/Mastery).\n+- Rejected spellings: none recorded in this lane (no wrong submission in any mode, days 1-7).\n - `knowledge.py`: `JPEG_DIMENSIONS_FMT`, `PNG_DIMENSIONS_FMT`, `PDF_HEADER_VERSION_FMT`, `BOOL`.\n - Inference: the field id IS the spec name (`sof_dimensions_pixels` = SOF frame header, `ihdr_` = IHDR chunk,\n   `header_version` = file header) — read the field name literally to pick which structure to parse.\n@@ -91,6 +109,8 @@ only one present in single; TT used `roster.csv`, Mastery a renamed `evidence-no\n - Single / TT: one zip, one member, member named in `artifact` after `->`.\n - Mastery days 1,2,4,5: ONE download named `...-evidence-01.zip` that is an outer zip containing `...-01.zip` and\n   `...-02.zip` (zip-of-zips); each inner zip holds its set's member.\n+- Mastery day 7: zip-of-zips again, three levels (outer `-01.zip` holds `-01.zip` + `-02.zip`, each holding the asked\n+  `evidence-drop-00N.zip`); artifact ref `metadata-day-07-evidence-0N.zip -> evidence-drop-00N.zip` (no `delivery N:`).\n - Mastery day 6: two downloads with identical filenames -> `delivery 1: <zip>` / `delivery 2: <zip>` in artifact refs.\n - Member numbering shifts between pre-fetched contract and live attempt (003/004 vs 006/007) — never hardcode names.\n \n@@ -99,6 +119,8 @@ only one present in single; TT used `roster.csv`, Mastery a renamed `evidence-no\n - Contract question text can be stale vs `answer_ids` (Day 2 TT): answer under `answer_ids`, locate the member that exists.\n - Don't let the flavor text widen the question: prompts mention impostors/passengers/orientation, but only the named\n   field is graded. Answer it; keep extra checks as diagnostics.\n+- Container-of-containers: when the asked file is itself a zip, a naive `rfind(PK\\x05\\x06)` on the downloaded evidence\n+  zip reads the OUTER EOCD (1 entry; Mastery outer says 2). Resolve the named member's bytes first, then parse.\n - Decoys by name: `*-with-bom.txt`, `.exe` that is text, `.bin` that is PDF, `.pdf` that is PNG — bytes win every time.\n - Timed windows are ~5-6 s and most of it is GM start/download/submit round-trips (solve ~0.1 s): never do anything slow\n   (extraction to disk, exiftool) in-window; parse in memory.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01YBxDqJqJgdnwjrMzetnKbP","agent_id":"aaed6392ab7d07d01","session_id":"a2624e74-c74a-41db-9965-6b2cb921c121","uuid":"f9124a10-9059-4e5f-bd5b-83c03e18dd51","timestamp":"2026-10-07T13:08:28.780Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"metadata day07 technique log"}
