{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfnvsgBYfmEL5xfVndHf8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I updated `reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md` for day 7. It's the only file I touched and is now 131 lines. I ran no `hctf` commands.\n\n**What day 7 was:** despite the \"Seven-Zip\" pun, the artifact was a plain ZIP; there was no 7z anywhere. The evidence zip held `evidence-drop-001.zip`, an uncompressed zip with two identical 48-byte text files. The question asked for that inner zip's end-of-central-directory (EOCD) total-entries count (`zip.eocd_total_entries`). The answer was `2`, CORRECT on the first submit 57 s after start. The prompt's \"census that does not add up\" and \"empty space\" never came up: in every variant, the EOCD count, the central-directory headers and the local headers all agreed.\n\n**Changes to the log:**\n- **Day 7 entry** added under `## Day by day`: the artifact, how the answer was read, the tools the worker used, timings, and the time trial / mastery results. Time trial answered `3` (0.89 s used of a 7 s window). Mastery answered `4` and `5` (1.33 s of 7 s). The pre-fetched mastery contract matched the live one this time.\n- **How challenges have looked:** days 1-7; the asked member can itself be a zip; added the new field to the list of field families; documented the answer-id spelling (`.` and `_` become `-`, e.g. `d07-zip-001-zip-eocd-total-entries`); first-submit solves now take ~30-60 s; titles are puns, not format hints.\n- **Variant axes:**\n  - Merged into \"Member and values\": the entry count goes up by one per variant (2/3/4/5 for drops 001-004).\n  - New axis \"Nesting depth\": mastery nested the asked zip three levels deep, so resolve it by the name after `->`.\n- **Recognition cues:** new `zip.eocd_*` row with the EOCD field offsets, ZIP64 handling and a cross-check by counting headers.\n- **Conventions:**\n  - Counts are a plain base-10 integer.\n  - The inference note now says `eocd_total_entries` means what the record claims, not a walk of the entries.\n  - Still no rejected spellings in this lane, days 1-7.\n- **Delivery layouts:** added the mastery day 7 three-level zip-of-zips; its artifact refs had no `delivery N:` prefix.\n- **Pitfalls:** searching the downloaded evidence zip for the EOCD reads the outer record (1 entry, or 2 on the mastery outer zip), so resolve the named inner zip first. Timed windows are now noted as ~5-7 s.\n\nNo solver case starts with `variant-*` and there is no `VARIANT AXIS:` line. All three `auto-*` and single cases match the confirmed answers.\n\n**GM-confirmed facts not yet in `lib/knowledge.py` / `lib/playbook.py`:**\n- `zip.eocd_total_entries` is the EOCD total-entries field (2-byte value at offset +10 of the `PK\\x05\\x06` record) of the zip named after `->`, submitted as a plain base-10 integer. Accepted values:\n  - `\"2\"` in `challenges/day07/metadata-seven-zip-no-relation/single_solve/submissions.jsonl`\n  - `\"3\"` in `.../time_trial/submissions.jsonl`\n  - `\"4\"` and `\"5\"` in `.../mastery/submissions.jsonl`\n- **Open question:** we still don't know whether the GM wants the claimed count or the actual entry count when the two differ, because they matched in every variant. Treat this as an open question rather than a confirmed rule.\n- No rejected spellings this day."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":292,"cache_read_input_tokens":62150,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":292,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01YBxDqJqJgdnwjrMzetnKbP","agent_id":"aaed6392ab7d07d01","session_id":"a2624e74-c74a-41db-9965-6b2cb921c121","uuid":"e5a0c864-5f3d-4784-b830-26b437fd472a","timestamp":"2026-10-07T13: