.\")\n# variant axes\nrep(\"- **HCFG location** -- same blob, different storage per container (`.hcfg` section, .NET FieldRVA, Go/Rust rodata,\\n  base64 inside a Java constant pool): scan the raw (and base64-decoded) bytes for `HCFG`, never a fixed offset.\",\n    \"- **HCFG location** -- same blob, different storage per container (`.hcfg` section, .NET FieldRVA, Go/Rust rodata,\\n  base64 inside a Java/Kotlin constant pool): scan the raw (and base64-decoded) bytes for `HCFG`, never a fixed offset.\")\nrep(\"- **Container per member** -- ELF vs MinGW PE32+ seen for the same C++ group; machine/format labels must come from the\\n  header of THIS member.\",\n    \"- **Container per member** -- ELF vs PE32+ `.exe` re-rolls per member: C++ d02 and Go d04 were `.exe` in Mastery set2 (D4, D5,\\n  D7; D6 set2 d04 was ELF). Labels come from the header of THIS member (Go PE: format `pe`, architecture `x86-64` from Machine).\\n- **Variant index per group** -- `dNN--variant-XXX` re-rolls per group and mode (D7 TT: d03-001, d04-006, d07-005 ...); sizes\\n  and config values change, names/layout don't. D7 TT bytes were identical to Mastery set1.\")\nrep(\"| `.jar` / \\\"constant pool\\\" | unzip the jar, read `META-INF/MANIFEST.MF` Main-Class, `javap -v -p Main.class`; look for `ConstantValue: String` (`static final String CONFIG`) |\",\n    \"| `.jar` / \\\"constant pool\\\" | unzip the jar, read `META-INF/MANIFEST.MF` Main-Class, `javap -v -p Main.class`; look for `ConstantValue: String` (`static final String CONFIG`) |\\n| Kotlin fat jar (`kotlin/` runtime, `META-INF/main.kotlin_module`, `X$fn$1 extends ContinuationImpl` with `int label`) | Same as `.jar`: parse the Main-Class first, skip `kotlin/`/`org/jetbrains/`. Coroutine \\\"state machine\\\" = `invokeSuspend` switching on `label`; branch logic is plain `javap -c` (`lookupswitch` on String.hashCode + `ldc` results) |\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF","description":"Apply header, axes, cue edits"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}