decoy`/7, sandbox→`failure`/3,\n  else `failure`/1; prints trace JSON `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1` {branch, event_count, campaign, family\n  `loopback_stage_transfer`}. If branch/event questions appear: read them statically from `javap -c`, never run the jar.\n- TT 5.8 s of an 11 s window, Mastery 6.4 s of 12 s, both first-try CORRECT (set2 had d02/d04 as PE `.exe`).\n\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old)==1; s=s.replace(old,new)\nold=\"| format (Java) | `jar` | jar_jvm |\"\nnew=\"| format (Java/Kotlin jar) | `jar` (D6 Java, D7 Kotlin) | jar_jvm |\"\nassert s.count(old)==1; s=s.replace(old,new)\nold=\"| architecture | the same machine words (Go amd64 → `x86-64`) | amd64, arm64, 386, x86_64 |\"\nnew=\"| architecture | the same machine words (Go ELF amd64 → `x86-64`; Go PE `.exe` 0x8664 → `x86-64`) | amd64, arm64, 386, x86_64 |\"\nassert s.count(old)==1; s=s.replace(old,new)\nold=\"- **Recursive unzip** destroys nested containers (.jar/.apk) and their `dNN--` prefix; keep them whole.\"\nnew=\"\"\"- **Recursive unzip** destroys nested containers (.jar/.apk) and their `dNN--` prefix; keep them whole.\n- **Jar members are deflated**: `grep HCFG file.jar` finds nothing. Inflate the class, read constant-pool strings, base64-decode.\n  In a fat jar (Kotlin/Scala/shaded) scan the Main-Class first; a full scan of ~3000 runtime classes eats timed windows.\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old)==1; s=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nwc -l reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md; git diff --stat reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md","description":"Add Day 7 entry, conventions, pitfalls"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2524,"cache_read_input_tokens":61187,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2524,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transforma