/binary-reverse-engineering.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":11,"oldLines":8,"newStart":11,"newLines":8,"lines":["   service, host_model on D7): parse the whole dict so a new `config_<key>` id is free."," - The analysis is easy (headers, symbols, one config blob). The hard part is the GM's exact label for a few `exact_text` fields (format,","   machine, disassembly, symbol). The question set grows each day (9 → 17 → 24 → 32 → 40 → 48 → 56 fields); old groups reuse the same bytes.","-- The prompt's theme (C++ RTTI, Rust panics, D7 \"coroutine state machine\") has NOT been asked since D3: the new group always got","-  the same 8 ids (sha256, format, config_campaign/domain/mutex/url/crc32_hex, hcfg_version). Read the ids before reversing logic.","+- The prompt's theme (Rust panics, D7 \"coroutine state machine\") has NOT been asked since D4: the new group always got 8 ids","+  (sha256, format, config_campaign/domain/mutex/url/crc32_hex, + architecture D4-D5 / hcfg_version D6-D7). Read the ids first."," - Time Trial ≈ 6-11 s, Mastery = `set1.`/`set2.` prefixed copies (≈ 7-12 s window); artifacts are named `delivery N: evidence.zip`."," "," ## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)"]},{"oldStart":88,"oldLines":6,"newStart":88,"newLines":17,"lines":[" - The D6 question text was REWRITTEN for formerly ambiguous fields: d01 disassembly now says \"Intel or AT&T spelling accepted\";","   d03 format says \"one container_runtime token; CLI, CLR or .NET accepted; separators/case accepted\". Read each question's full text and `syntax`."," ","+**D7 \"Routine Check\"** (56 Qs; 3 min start→CORRECT, 1 POST, 0 wrong). New d07 = `d07--variant-000.jar`, a 5 MB Kotlin fat jar","+(Main-Class `Day07Variant000`, class major 65, ~3300 entries incl. the kotlin/ runtime). d01-d06 bytes identical to D6 (sha256 match).","+- `javap -v -p Day07Variant000.class` → `private static final String CONFIG` ConstantValue base64 → HCFG (ver 1, key 0x31, len 368,","+  crc32 checked). Answers: format `jar` (again), config values verbatim, hcfg_version `1`. Copied the D6 solver; only change: jar","+  scan visits the Main-Class first and runtime packages last, returning at the first valid HCFG (the full scan was slow).","+- Unasked \"state machine\": `staged$1 extends ContinuationImpl {int label; Object L$0}`; `main` reads env `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL`","+  (default `workstation`) → `evaluate()` lookupswitch: workstation→`success`/13 events, analysis→`decoy`/7, sandbox→`failure`/3,","+  else `failure`/1; prints trace JSON `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1` {branch, event_count, campaign, family","+  `loopback_stage_transfer`}. If branch/event questions appear: read them statically from `javap -c`, never run the jar.","+- TT 5.8 s of an 11 s window, Mastery 6.4 s of 12 s, both first-try CORRECT (set2 had d02/d04 as PE `.exe`).","+"," ## GM answer conventions learned"," | Field family | Accepted form | Rejected (never resubmit) |"," |---|---|---|"]},{"oldStart":95,"oldLines":7,"newStart":106,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | endianness | `little` / `big` | little endian, lsb, msb |"," | machine (ELF) | `x86-64`, `x86`, `AArch64`, `ARM` | EM_X86_64, x86_64, amd64 |"," | machine (PE FILE_HEADER) | 0x14c → `i386`; 0x8664 → `x86-64` | x86 (for PE i386); raw `0x8664` |","-| architecture | the same machine words (Go amd64 → `x86-64`) | amd64, arm64, 386, x86_64 |","+| architecture | the same machine words (Go ELF amd64 → `x86-64`; Go PE `.exe` 0x8664 → `x86-64`) | amd64, arm64, 386, x86_64 |"," | elf_type | the constant `ET_EXEC` / `ET_DYN` | EXEC |"," | entry_point, crc32_hex, xor_key_hex | lowercase hex with `0x` (crc `0x%08x`, key `0x%02x`) | — |"," | recover_code | base-10 integer (`mov eax, 0x1fa4` → 8100); `none` if the named function is absent and the format allows it (inferred) | the renamed function's constant |"]},{"oldStart":103,"oldLines":7,"newStart":114,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | marker | exact `.huntress` string without the NUL; `none` if the section is missing | — |"," | format (native) | lowercase container: `elf`, `pe` (`macho` presumed) | ELF, ELF64, elf64-x86-64, HCFG, json, exe, pe32+, coff, mz |"," | format (.NET) | `pe_cli` | ~50 synonyms (pe, pe32, dotnet, .net, cil, msil, clr, managed, assembly, ...) — lib/knowledge.py DOTNET_FORMAT_REJECTED |","-| format (Java) | `jar` | jar_jvm |","+| format (Java/Kotlin jar) | `jar` (D6 Java, D7 Kotlin) | jar_jvm |"," | C++ symbols (ELF) | bare Itanium mangled name (`_ZNK...`, `_ZTV...`) | the demangled form |"," | C++ symbols (PE/MinGW) | COMDAT section name `.text$<mangled>` (function), `.rdata$<mangled>` (vtable) | bare mangled name |"," | section_names (JSON) | pyelftools order INCLUDING the leading `\"\"` | list without \"\" |"]},{"oldStart":125,"oldLines":6,"newStart":136,"newLines":8,"lines":[" - **Cumulative zip**: check whether the old groups' sha256 match a previous day's confirmed bytes. If yes, those answers carry over;","   spend the time on the NEW group only (D4-D6 took minutes because of this)."," - **Recursive unzip** destroys nested containers (.jar/.apk) and their `dNN--` prefix; keep them whole.","+- **Jar members are deflated**: `grep HCFG file.jar` finds nothing. Inflate the class, read constant-pool strings, base64-decode.","+  In a fat jar (Kotlin/Scala/shaded) scan the Main-Class first; a full scan of ~3000 runtime classes eats timed windows."," - **Stripped builds** in variants (D1 slot, D2 Mastery set2): no recover_code symbol. Use the leaf `mov eax, imm; ret` fallback, and has_symtab=false."," - **Renamed designated function** (D1 TT section-beacon): the question still says recover_code. Answer `none` (when the format allows it), not the other function's constant."," - **Tool parity** (2026-10-07): ilspycmd, dotnet, rustfilt, GoReSym (`GoReSym -t -p file`), rabin2 are installed in"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/challenges/day07/worker-ratchet-local-20261007T210620.log","/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md"],"shared":true}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfnvvuSbm54USGPuHHW8u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014kXVNg77Gv9EBQmZ2jLMVp","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; cat > $TMPDIR/samp.py <<'EOF'\nimport sys,os,re,json,base64\nsys.path.insert(0,'/home/testpwn/huntress-2026')\nfrom lib import codec\nseen=set()\nfor root in sys.argv[1:]:\n  for dp,dn,fn in os.walk(root):\n    for f in sorted(fn):\n      if f.endswith('.zip'): continue\n      t=open(os.path.join(dp,f),encoding='utf-8',errors='ignore').read()\n      for c in codec.find_codecs(t):\n        if c['plain']: continue\n        k=(c['rep'],c['transform'])\n        if k in seen: continue\n        seen.add(k)\n        m=c['material']; rep=c['rep']; tr=c['transform']; key=c['key']\n        if rep=='unicode_escapes': data=bytes(int(x,16) for x in re.findall(r'u([0-9a-fA-F]{4})',m))\n        elif rep=='json_numbers': data=bytes(json.loads(m.replace('\\\\\"','\"')))\n        elif rep=='reversed_base64': data=codec.b64(m[::-1])\n        elif rep=='xor_hex': data=bytes(b^int(tr,16) for b in bytes.fromhex(m)); tr='identity'\n        else: data={'base64_literal':codec.b64,'hex_compact':codec.hex_bytes}.get(rep, lambda x: None)(m)\n        if data is None and rep=='decimal_csv': data=bytes(codec.int_array(m,10))\n        if data is None and rep=='percent_hex': data=bytes.fromhex(m.replace('%',''))\n        outs=[b for b in codec._transform_candidates(tr or 'identity', key, data) if codec.looks_like_plan(b)] if data else []\n        print(f, '|', c['rep']+'|'+c['transform']+'|'+(c['key'] or ''), '|', m[:40], '->', outs[0][:60] if outs else ('RAW',data[:40] if data else None))\nEOF\n.venv/bin/python -I $TMPDIR/samp.py $TMPDIR/d7codecs challenges/day07/scripting-node-by-node/single_solve/work/extracted","description":"Produce sample decodes for new reps"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_seq