{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfnw7rKeGc6gNJXP9Y1wQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've updated `/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/script-analysis.md`; it is now 174 lines. I edited no other file and ran no `hctf` command.\n\n**What I changed in the log**\n- **Header:** covers days 1-7 now. Day 7 added 8 Node.js `.mjs` files and 2 Bash \"advanced syntax\" files, for 469 ids. Time Trial windows are now 5-13 s. Mastery on day 7 was one download containing both `evidence-01.zip` and `evidence-02.zip`.\n- **Variant axes:**\n  - Merged into \"Codec per file\": new rep names appear only in the timed variants, so decode by the material's shape, not its name.\n  - New axis \"Codec spec arity\": specs come as `rep|transform|key`, as `rep|` (empty transform means identity), or as `xor_hex|cd` (the key is the second field).\n  - New axis \"Reversal level\": some reps reverse the decoded list, while `reversed_base64` reverses the text before decoding.\n  - New axis \"Adapter values\": these change between variants even when the role is the same.\n- **Recognition cues:**\n  - New `.mjs` row (decode statically, never run it).\n  - New Bash `Feature_<id>()` row (role `advanced_syntax`).\n  - On the `evidence.zip` row: triage skipped `.mjs` files entirely, so compare the extracted files against the contract's artifact names.\n- **Codec table and role tables:** added the day-7 reps and the empty-transform form. Added the steps-to-role rows for `persistence_descriptor` and `advanced_syntax`. Node now follows the JScript rule (T1059.007). `schedule_path`, `service_name`, `feature` and `primitive` are copied verbatim from the plan.\n- **Day 7 entry:** single solve took about 100 s and was right first submit (469/469).\n  - **Time Trial** took three attempts. The first missed 15 ids because of the new reps. The second (26b7da83) received a 24-byte `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` saved as `evidence.zip`; I confirmed this from `time_trial/attempts/26b7da83` (size and sha256 differ from the contract). The third (516aa6d1) was CORRECT with 9.5 s used of the 11 s window.\n  - **Mastery** (2c52d50f) was CORRECT first try, using 3.9 s of 13 s.\n- **Pitfalls:**\n  - Added \"GM error body saved as the artifact\": check size and sha256 against the contract before solving.\n  - Added \"unknown rep name leaves fields unanswered\".\n  - Added the day-7 timing numbers to the transport-race entry.\n- **Correction to `solver/NOTES.md`:** its \"VARIANT AXIS: none\" is wrong. It came from the second generalize worker, which only looked at the rate-limited attempt. The first worker found the new reps. I recorded the lesson to diagnose every failed attempt, not just the latest.\n- **Older day entries (D1-D6):** shortened to make room.\n\n**GM-confirmed facts missing from `lib/knowledge.py` / `lib/playbook.py`:** none. Your uncommitted edits to those files already cover persistence_descriptor = T1053.003 whatever the adapter, advanced_syntax = T1059.004, the Node role table, and the feature/primitive values. Every timed answer used the same spellings as single (`single_solve/confirmed.json`, `time_trial/confirmed.json`, `mastery/confirmed.json`). There were no rejected spellings: each mode was correct on its one submit.\n\n**New codec reps and transforms not handled by `lib/codec.py`.** In this case `find_codecs` failed on 26 of 336 codecs, all handled by `_material_readings` / `fallback_plan` in `challenges/day07/scripting-node-by-node/solver/solve.py`:\n- `unicode_escapes` (Node): `\\u0076\\u003d\\u0031…` with identity gives `v=1|steps=decode_embedded,write_file|…`. It also appeared with `subtract_modulo_256|0c` and `rolling_xor|d2`.\n- `json_numbers` (Node): `[118,61,49,124,…]` with identity gives `v=1|steps=…`. It also appeared with `reverse_then_xor|9b`, `add_modulo_256|08`, `reverse_bytes` and `repeating_key_xor|3e,5a,c5,74,55`.\n- `reversed_base64|` (Bash): `==AduVGdul2X0NWd…`, with the text reversed and then base64-decoded, gives `v=1|feature=indirect_expansion|…`.\n- `xor_hex|cd` (Bash): `bbf0fcb1…`, hex-decoded and XORed with 0xcd, gives `v=1|feature=indirect_expansion|…`.\n- **Empty-transform arity `rep|`**: `decode()` returns None when the transform field is empty instead of treating it as identity. Seen as `base64_literal|`, `hex_compact|`, `decimal_csv|` and `percent_hex|` (`%76%3d%31…` gives `v=1|feature=…`).\n\n`lib/codec.py` already decodes `hex_buffer`, `hex_array`, `escaped_octets` and `decimal_array` through its generic readings, but those names are not in its `REPS` list."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":787,"cache_read_input_tokens":122282,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":787,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":789,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gsx5nZnpi34d3BX6KLkfsy","agent_id":"a5ec04f78cf4f7c93","session_id":"a2624e74-c74a-41db-9965-6b2cb921c121","uuid":"5364ec96-c218-4f5f-a089-850752eee92e","timestamp":"2026-10-07T13:12:07.657Z","request_id":"req_011Cfnw7r1XxJnqfWRZxv15D","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"script day07 technique log"}
